maya: Heads-up — I hit a schema mismatch between the API reference and actual /v1/generate streaming responses after the streaming proto change. Docs example shows choices[].delta.tokens but the runtime emits choices[].delta.text. This will break the Python/Go SDK snippets.

maya: Example from docs currently:```json
{"choices": [{"delta": {"tokens": "hello"}}]}
```

maya: Actual payload we see in logs/trace:```json
{"choices": [{"delta": {"text": "hello"}}]}
```

maya: Filing a quick PR to update examples + migration note: https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/12678 — but need a quick review and confirmation this is the canonical shape (cc @sarah @tj).

tj: Thanks for flagging. I can confirm runtime now uses `delta.text` for streaming deltas (we consolidated token->text across languages last week). docs PR looks small. Will review in ~30m. :thumbsup:

sarah: Also check embedding and chunked-rerank examples. Some SDK snippets assume `delta.tokens` in the iterator. We should add a one-liner migration note at top of endpoint doc: "Streaming clients: use delta.text (or fallback to delta.tokens)".

maya: Good call. I added a short migration blurb in the PR description, but not in the page yet. Would prefer explicit example for Go + Python showing defensive access.

maya: Proposed Python snippet update:
```python
# previously
for chunk in resp.iter_chunks():
    token = chunk.choices[0].delta.get("tokens")
    if token:
        out += token
# update
for chunk in resp.iter_chunks():
    text = chunk.choices[0].delta.get("text") or chunk.choices[0].delta.get("tokens")
    if text:
        out += text
```

tj: LGTM. For Go, do something like:```go
// old
if deltaTokens := chunk.Choices[0].Delta["tokens"]; deltaTokens != nil {
    out += deltaTokens.(string)
}
// new
if deltaText := chunk.Choices[0].Delta["text"]; deltaText != nil {
    out += deltaText.(string)
} else if deltaTokens := chunk.Choices[0].Delta["tokens"]; deltaTokens != nil {
    out += deltaTokens.(string)
}
```

doc-bot: CI docs build ✅ for branch docs-update/delta-text-examples (staging URL: https://docs-staging.redwood.ai/streaming#generate).

maya: Great. @tj can you approve and merge after a quick linter pass? Also can someone add a tiny regression test to the docs spec that checks sample response contains `delta.text`? That'll catch regressions if runtime flips again.

tj: On it. I'll add the test and merge. I'll also open a follow-up to add a short compatibility note in the migration guide and flag Dedicated customers in the release notes.

sarah: Please ping #eng-runtime if we need to revert or add compatibility layer. Also file a short changelog entry so Support can email a few customers if needed.

maya: Thanks all — assigning follow-ups: tj -> merge + test, sarah -> changelog blurb, maya -> add compatibility note to migration guide. Will monitor staging after merge.

